{"name":"Cat Person","hex":"#636d70","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Catalan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Terms relating to animals.\n  A mammal of the family Felidae.","A mammal of the family Felidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cat"},{"term":"person","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An individual who has been granted personhood; usually a human being. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A character or part, as in a play; a specific kind or manifestation of individual character, whether in real life, or in literary or dramatic representation; an assumed character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To represent as a person; to personify; to impersonate.","To man, to supply with staff or crew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/person"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cat Person","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cat Person\" is a short story by Kristen Roupenian that was first published in December 2017 in The New Yorker before going viral online. The BBC described the short story as \"being shared widely online as social media users discuss how much it relates to modern-day dating\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/03/Cat_Person_lead_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat_Person","wikidata":"Q48741999"},{"title":"Cat Person (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cat Person is a 2023 psychological thriller film directed by Susanna Fogel from a screenplay by Michelle Ashford, based on the 2017 short story of the same name by Kristen Roupenian. The film stars Emilia Jones, Nicholas Braun, Geraldine Viswanathan, Hope Davis, Fred Melamed, and Isabella Rossellini."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/Cat_person_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat_Person_(film)","wikidata":"Q109284836"},{"title":"Cat people and dog people","blocks":[{"text":"The terms cat people and dog people refer to a person's domesticated pet animal preference. Through research completed at research institutions, it was found that there were differences in character and behaviour between those who prefer cats and those who prefer dogs. It was also found that some people base a significant portion of their identity around their affinity for either cats or dogs. This builds on the perceived dichotomy between cats and dogs as pets in society. In some cases, the two terms refer to people's self-identification, regardless of what pets they actually own, if any."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Cat_v_Dog_voting_bin_-_April_2023.jpg/330px-Cat_v_Dog_voting_bin_-_April_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat_people_and_dog_people","wikidata":"Q25099789"},{"title":"Cat","blocks":[{"text":"The cat, also called domestic cat and house cat, is a small domesticated carnivorous mammal. It is a member of Felidae, the family of mammals in the order Carnivora also colloquially referred to as cats. An obligate carnivore requiring a predominantly meat-based diet, it has retractable claws adapted to killing small prey species such as mice and rats. It has a strong, flexible body, quick reflexes, and sharp teeth, and its night vision and sense of smell are well developed. It is a social species, but a solitary hunter and a crepuscular predator.\nCat communication includes meowing, purring, trilling, hissing, growling, grunting, body language, and scent marking. It can hear sounds too faint or too high in frequency for human ears, such as those made by small mammals. It secretes and perceives pheromones. Cat intelligence is evident in its ability to adapt, learn through observation, and solve problems. The domestic cat is the only domesticated species of the family Felidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Siam_lilacpoint.jpg/330px-Siam_lilacpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat","wikidata":"Q146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Sheba1.JPG/500px-Sheba1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Sheba1.JPG/500px-Sheba1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASheba1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Cat_August_2010-4.jpg/500px-Cat_August_2010-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Cat_August_2010-4.jpg/1280px-Cat_August_2010-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Cat_August_2010-4.jpg/500px-Cat_August_2010-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACat_August_2010-4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Felis_catus-cat_on_snow.jpg/500px-Felis_catus-cat_on_snow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Felis_catus-cat_on_snow.jpg/500px-Felis_catus-cat_on_snow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFelis_catus-cat_on_snow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Gustav_chocolate.jpg/500px-Gustav_chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org